     <article class="story single" data-beat="finance">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">FINANCE</span> · Livemint Money · 2026-10-11 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>8th Central Pay Commission Schedules Mumbai Consultations</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#finance</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The 8th Central Pay Commission, chaired by Justice Ranjana Prakash Desai, will hold stakeholder consultations in Mumbai on October 22–23, 2026. The commission is gathering input from employee unions, pensioner associations, and federations to finalize recommendations on salary structures, allowances, and retirement benefits for over 1 crore central government employees and pensioners.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-11/8th-central-pay-commission-schedules-mumbai-consultations.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>During the Mumbai visit, the panel will specifically observe railway operations, including track maintenance and signal duties, to assess working conditions. This commission, constituted by Prime Minister Narendra Modi last year, is currently in the consultation stage and previously concluded data submission windows in July. Interested parties must apply for appointments by October 10.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate summary of the upcoming 8th CPC meetings and the commission's scope.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.livemint.com/money/8th-pay-commission-what-are-the-upcoming-state-visit-dates-22-23-october-check-agenda-pay-allowances-pensions-benefits-11791719804508.html" rel="noopener">Livemint Money</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/mumbai/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mumbai</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
