       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-11 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Hyderabad Hosts Cyclothon for Arthritis Awareness</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Yashoda Hospitals organized a cyclothon titled 'Pedal for Arthritis Awareness' in Hyderabad on Sunday to promote joint health and physical activity. Over 500 participants cycled from the hospital's Secunderabad facility to Necklace Road ahead of World Arthritis Day on October 12.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-11/hyderabad-hosts-cyclothon-for-arthritis-awareness.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Director Pavan Gorukanti and orthopaedic surgeon Vikram Byre led the initiative, emphasizing that early diagnosis and regular exercise are vital for managing arthritis. The event encouraged the public to adopt active lifestyles and seek timely medical care to improve quality of life, noting that the condition affects an estimated 195 million people in India across all age groups.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate and appropriately dense summary of the event.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/cities/Hyderabad/cyclothon-held-in-hyderabad-to-raise-awareness-on-arthritis/article71571473.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
