     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-11 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Minister V. Somanna to Review Railway Projects in Shivamogga</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Union Minister of State for Railways and Jal Shakti V. Somanna will visit Shivamogga on Monday to conduct a review meeting regarding local railway projects. The session, held at the city's Circuit House, will include Lok Sabha member B.Y. Raghavendra and senior South Western Railway officials.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-11/minister-v-somanna-to-review-railway-projects-in-shivamogga.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Discussions are expected to cover the proposed Shivamogga-Shikaripur-Ranebennur railway line, the potential upgrade of Bhadravathi railway station, and the construction of a coaching depot at Koteganguru. Following the meeting, the Minister is scheduled to inspect road underbridge construction work near Birur.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Correctly summarizes the upcoming visit and project topics.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/karnataka/v-somanna-to-hold-meeting-on-railway-projects-in-shivamogga/article71571065.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
