       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · BBC Sport · 2026-10-11 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Sale beats Harlequins 28-24 to extend losing streak</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#sports</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Harlequins suffered their third consecutive loss of the Prem season after falling 28-24 to Sale at CorpAcq Stadium. Despite an early lead fueled by two Marcus Smith tries, Quins were ultimately overcome by a 73rd-minute penalty try.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-11/sale-beats-harlequins-28-24-to-extend-losing-streak.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The victory marks back-to-back wins for Sale following their opening-day defeat to Bristol. Conversely, the result leaves Harlequins winless and rooted to the bottom of the table. Sale's scoring included tries from Canakaivata, Warr, and Bamber, alongside three conversions by Ford, while Harlequins also saw two tries from Riley.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is accurate and captures the essential match details within the requested length.</p>
