     <article class="story single" data-beat="sports">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · NDTV Sports · 2026-10-11 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Shane Watson Criticizes India's Squad Rotation Policy</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#sports</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Former Chennai Super Kings star Shane Watson has criticized India's head coach Gautam Gambhir for frequent squad changes following India's defeat to the West Indies in the second T20I. Watson noted that while player rotation is necessary for workload management, the current lack of continuity is negatively impacting team performance and synergy.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-11/shane-watson-criticizes-indias-squad-rotation-policy.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Critics argue that constant reshuffling disrupts player confidence and role clarity. Conversely, supporters of the strategy suggest that Gambhir is focused on building resilient bench strength and testing tactical combinations ahead of major ICC tournaments. Achieving a balance between necessary rest and maintaining a stable core remains a central challenge for the team.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Effectively summarizes the criticism and the counter-arguments regarding squad rotation while maintaining the source's tone.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://sports.ndtv.com/cricket/csk-great-targets-gautam-gambhir-over-indias-inconsistent-run-too-much-chopping-and-changing-12168722#publisher=newsstand" rel="noopener">NDTV Sports</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
