       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-11 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Shigella Cluster Reported in Thrissur District</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Health authorities in Thrissur, Kerala, are monitoring a cluster of 10 Shigella infections reported in early October. Seven cases, including a seven-month-old infant, have been linked to a temple festival in Tholur, where the infection source was identified as a ritual well that has since been chlorinated.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-11/shigella-cluster-reported-in-thrissur-district.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>All patients are recovering or have already recovered. This outbreak coincides with a broader surge in fever cases, with nearly 5,000 people seeking treatment between October 1 and 9. Additionally, health officials confirmed 39 cases of dengue and four cases of leptospirosis, prompting increased surveillance across the district.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is accurate, though it misses the specific detail that the Wadakkanchery, Arimbur, and Adat cases were separate from the Tholur cluster.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/kerala/shigella-cases-ring-alarm-bells-in-thrissur-as-10-infections-surface-in-nine-days/article71568228.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/thrissur/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Thrissur</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
