       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-11 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Two killed in separate Bengaluru road accidents</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Two individuals died in separate motorcycle accidents in Bengaluru on Sunday, with police confirming that neither victim wore a helmet. Namay Sharma, a Delhi native, died after crashing his motorcycle into a flyover retaining wall in the Madiwala traffic limits.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-11/two-killed-in-separate-bengaluru-road-accidents.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>In a second incident, 30-year-old cook Ganga Yadav was killed when his scooter struck a tree near the Outer Ring Road. His pillion rider sustained serious injuries during the crash. Both cases are currently under investigation by local traffic police authorities.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate reporting of all key facts, including the victims' names and circumstances of the accidents.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
