       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-11 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Volunteers remove waste from Tiruvannamalai forest land</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Over 500 volunteers removed more than one tonne of garbage, primarily PET bottles, from forest lands along the Girivalam path on Sunday. The effort was part of the &quot;Clean Tiruvannamalai&quot; initiative, launched by Collector Vandhana Garg to prepare the town for the upcoming Karthigai Deepam festival.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-11/volunteers-remove-waste-from-tiruvannamalai-forest-land.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The project involved a collaboration between the district administration, the Forest Department, and local organizations. Officials confirmed the cleanup was initiated following a formal request from the Forest Department to address waste accumulation. Volunteers plan to maintain the path through regular cleaning sessions scheduled twice a month.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Comprehensive and accurate coverage of the clean-up event and the details provided in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
