       <h1>Wales Forward Elise Hughes Focused on Albania Play-off</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#sports</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Wales forward Elise Hughes has described reaching the World Cup as a lifelong ambition but insists the team’s immediate focus is Tuesday’s play-off second leg against Albania. Wales carries a 1-0 lead into the Llanelli fixture, with a draw sufficient to advance the team to the next qualifying stage.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-11/wales-forward-elise-hughes-focused-on-albania-play-off.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Should Wales progress, they face a two-legged final against either Norway or Romania in December, followed by a potential inter-confederation play-off in February. Head coach Rhian Wilkinson noted that despite the first-leg victory in Shkoder, the team must improve their performance to ensure they secure the result needed to continue their qualification campaign.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is accurate, concise, and correctly captures the status of the play-off and Hughes' comments.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
